# /mode jev-on with a Jev key but no generator key (a fake TYPESAFE_API_KEY, JEVCODE_ASSERT_NO_NETWORK=1; started with `--mode jev-only`,
# TUI-DESIGN-3 §1.10): the wizard's provider step opens in place (`jev+llm needs a generator. Pick the provider:`); Ctrl-C closes it —
# never exits — and the mode stays jev-only (TUI-DESIGN-2 §1.3, §1.4, §8.2 mode-switch)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
sleep 0.2
send /mode jev-on
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect Pick the provider
sleep 0.3
send \x03
expect mode stays jev-only
expect jev-only
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
